\begin{abstract}
This notebook reconstructs explicit mathematical maps suggested by earlier
polynomial, arithmetic, and fluid calculations. It also develops selected
mechanisms from the released smooth-forcing Euler and Boussinesq work, retaining
the additional terms produced by positive viscosity. Every result proved here
is stated at its actual scope. No counterexample to the classical
three-dimensional Navier--Stokes problem has been established by this notebook.
The reported separate classical Navier--Stokes proof has not been obtained.
The notebook makes no prize claim. Attribution follows identifiable sources;
it does not assign unverified contributions to a named person.
